{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784572760,"nonce":"iB7J0FmkB7xxqgKSt3LvsVyFl0Q=","title":"Implements ADR-0057 — the PR provenance slice. Reference the ADR for locked decisions.","message":"A `pull_request`-triggered run shows the **PR title** as its headline and reads `base ← head` in the ref/commit cluster. Reuses the `trigger_title` plumbing and shared Trigger-cell component from slice A.\n\n- `Event::PullRequest` gains `title: String` and `base: String` (from `pull_request.title` / `pull_request.base.ref`); both adapters parse them; extend adapter payload fixtures.\n- `base` is a **discrete origin fact**, not folded into `trigger_title`: new nullable column `runs.origin_pr_base TEXT` (sibling of `origin_pr_number`), stamped alongside origin. `title` flows through `trigger_title(event)` (subject-style 200-char cap) for `pull_request` kind.\n- The new fields must NOT enter `Event::context()` (same boundary as slice A).\n- DTOs gain the PR base (`origin_pr_base: Option\u003cString\u003e`); threaded onto the run read models. Regenerate OpenAPI + UI schema.\n- UI: the shared Trigger cell renders the PR title as the headline; the ref cluster renders `base ← head` on PR runs.\n\n\n- [ ] A fresh PR run persists `trigger_title` = PR title and `origin_pr_base` = base ref (verified via API + list DTO).\n- [ ] Both GitHub and Forgejo adapter tests parse title + base from fixtures.\n- [ ] `Event::context()` does not expose `title`/`base` (test asserts absence).\n- [ ] UI: a PR run shows `pull_request` + PR title in the Trigger cell and `base ← head` in the ref cluster; non-PR runs are unaffected.\n- [ ] `just check` + targeted `cargo test` green; OpenAPI regenerated.\n\n\n- [adr-0057] Push commit-subject headline end-to-end (slice A) — provides the `trigger_title` column, extractor/stamp, DTO field, and shared Trigger-cell component.","files":null}]}